00:15:15,471 --> 00:15:18,519
in the rehearsal copy, and the recovery.

211
00:15:18,859 --> 00:15:22,566
Before the fix, list the candidate
fixes and give each its rung.

212
00:15:22,606 --> 00:15:27,131
Before each verification command, write
the output you predict and the reason.

213
00:15:27,171 --> 00:15:31,872
In the failure scenario, predict what the
abort will discard and from which layer

214
00:15:31,912 --> 00:15:36,497
each part can be returned. The lab's
questions are answered in a separate file.

215
00:15:36,537 --> 00:15:37,609
Attempt them first.

216
00:15:37,949 --> 00:15:42,827
The challenge has no file: take three
entries of the symptom catalog in section

217
00:15:42,867 --> 00:15:47,871
29.11 at random and say, without the book,
the first three read-only commands for

218
00:15:47,911 --> 00:15:48,929
each. Then check.

219
00:15:52,769 --> 00:15:56,113
Answer out loud. The
justification is what is scored.

220
00:15:56,153 --> 00:16:01,221
A strong answer doesn't rank by feeling.
It applies stated criteria to each fix:

221
00:16:01,261 --> 00:16:06,328
what can it destroy, whom does it affect,
how is it undone, can it be previewed.

222
00:16:06,368 --> 00:16:11,500
It places each of the five on the ladder
and explains ties and near-ties, because

223
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,607
two of them sit on the same rung.

224
00:16:13,947 --> 00:16:18,704
It names the one that combines two rungs
and says which of its two halves does which

225
00:16:18,744 --> 00:16:23,501
damage. And it adds the condition that
changes the ranking: whether the working tree

226
00:16:23,541 --> 00:16:26,242
is clean, and whether the
commits are published.

227
00:16:28,082 --> 00:16:29,010
Let's land this.

228
00:16:29,350 --> 00:16:34,028
Candidate fixes are ranked by what they
can destroy: uncommitted work, published

229
00:16:34,068 --> 00:16:36,918
history, the server,
undoability, previewability.

230
00:16:37,258 --> 00:16:41,542
The ladder runs from adding a ref to removing
the safety net; take the lowest rung

231
00:16:41,582 --> 00:16:42,755
that repairs the cause.

232
00:16:43,095 --> 00:16:48,582
On shared branches revert; move refs back
with --keep; force only with an explicit

233
00:16:48,622 --> 00:16:49,593
expected value.

234
00:16:49,933 --> 00:16:54,693
Verification is four checks: the symptom,
the state, every copy, nothing else

235
00:16:54,733 --> 00:16:57,560
changed, each with a
prediction written first.

236
00:16:57,900 --> 00:17:02,120
Nearly every symptom in the catalog is a
difference between two places that someone

237
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,095
assumed were equal.

238
00:17:04,935 --> 00:17:10,815
